Thursday Update
Trade Alert: Buy MMM calls Stocks slump as jobs data disappoints and bond y=
ields riseStocks are falling with oil futures amid concern over a surprise =
increase in initial jobless claims. At the same time, Treasury yields have =
returned pre-pandemic levels.The Dow Jones Industrial Average fell by 262 p=
oints, or 0.8%, while the S&amp;P 500 was down 0.9% to 3,894.96 and Nasdaq =
was lower by 1.4%. Energy and technology were among the steepest decliners,=
 with all sectors but utilities in the red at midday.Initial jobless claims=
 rose to 861,000 in the week ended Feb. 13 from 848,000 the previous week a=
nd compared with an expected decline to 773,000, as per data compiled by Bl=
oomberg."Last week's claims were revised up by 55,000, which explains much =
of the overshoot to consensus this week," a report from Pantheon Macroecono=
mics said. "We expect to see a sustainable downward trend emerge over the n=
ext couple months as the economy gradually reopens, but claims likely will =
be temporarily boosted by the extraordinarily severe weather across much of=
 the country this week."The US 10-year yield slipped by 1.4 basis points to=
 1.29%, the highest level since February 2020.The probability of a 25 basis=
-point increase in the Fed funds rate to a range of 25-50 basis points stoo=
d at more than 12% currently, compared with just over 2% as of Feb. 11, acc=
ording to the CME Group's FedWatch Tool."While the 10-year has had a strong=
 run since August-September of last year, the longer-term monthly charts st=
ill show the potential for further mean reversion higher - where we believe=
 the TNX [Treasury Yield 10 Years] can trade toward the 1.50%+ range at som=
e point this year," according to a technical analysis report from Janney.In=
 company news, Walmart (WMT) expects sales growth in its new fiscal year to=
 slow as the retail giant closed out its fiscal 2021 with record sales driv=
en by the COVID-19 pandemic. Shares fell by 5.5% intraday, the worst perfor=
mer on the Dow.Baidu (BIDU) on Wednesday reported a decline in its adjusted=
 earnings per American depository shares in the fourth quarter even as reve=
nue increased from a year ago. The stock was the steepest decliner on Nasda=
q, down by 5.3%. FirstEnergy (FE) shares jumped by 7.6%, the most on S&amp;=
P 500, after the company reported that it swung to profit in the fourth qua=
rter even as sales declined from a year ago.Portfolio: We came into today f=
lat because our order for HD calls did not fill. We have one new idea for y=
ou.*CURRENT RECOMMENDATIONS3M Corp. (MMM) March 180 calls-- Symbol: MMM2103=
19C00180000-- Order: Buy at $4.20 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell =
half at $5.50 lmt gtc and half at $7.20 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $2=
.95 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only\*Thanks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAl=
l recommendations are for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of t=
he specified month unless otherwise noted. All stops are good after 10:30 a=
.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. All orders are good for the da=
y only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at the close of the=
 current session. Past results are no guarantee of future returns. All acco=
unts may not achieve comparable results. Recommendations are leveraged and =
speculative, so only use risk capital =E2=80=94 i.e., money you can afford =
to lose. All results are shown ex-commissions and fees. Options trading inv=
olves the risk of substantial loss. Some news and research provided by Wall=
 Street Journal, Bloomberg, Associated Press, MT Newswires and Reuters.&nbs=
p;

